3	// / hybrid), resolves engines at runtime, and either passes through to a single
4	// engine or orchestrates a hybrid round-trip.
5	//
6	// This file owns argument dispatch and the help TREE: which commands exist,
7	// what each is for, and one runnable example set per command. The options
8	// themselves are described once, in options.cpp, and printed from there.
